    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, I’m Dr. ____. What brings you in today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S014",
      "patient_response": "Hi, Doc. Yeah, so, I’m here because... well, it’s kind of a lot, to be honest. I’m a firefighter, right? Which you’d think is the perfect job for a guy who likes to be on the go. And I do, I really do. But lately, it’s like... I just feel like I’m always running hot. Like, physically and mentally, just running at maximum capacity all the time. It’s like I have this engine inside me and I just can’t shut the motor off, no matter what I do or how exhausted I should be. \n\nEven when we’re back at the station and it’s supposed to be downtime, you know, when the other guys are just kicking back in the recliners, watching TV or trying to catch some sleep between calls, I just can't do it. I’m pacing the bays, or finding equipment to reorganize that doesn't need reorganizing, or just talking everyone’s ear off when they're trying to rest. And, well, that’s the main reason I finally made this appointment, because lately, that exact thing has been getting me in real trouble at the firehouse. My captain actually pulled me aside—I think it was Tuesday after a 24-hour shift—and he basically told me I'm driving the rest of the crew crazy and I need to get a handle on it. I just can't seem to power down, ever, and it's starting to mess with my job.",
