    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Have you also been feeling unusually euphoric or overly high in your mood, not just restless or on edge?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Euphoric? Like... really happy or on top of the world? No, no, definitely not that. I mean, don't get me wrong, sometimes you get that rush, right? Like if we have a really intense call, maybe a structure fire or a bad MVA—motor vehicle accident, you know—and everyone does their job perfectly and everyone goes home safe, sure, you feel great for a bit. You get that massive adrenaline dump. But that’s just normal job stuff, and it fades. \n\nWhat I’m dealing with on a daily basis, especially when we're just sitting around the station... it’s not a happy feeling at all. I'm not walking around feeling like Superman or like I'm in some unusually fantastic mood. It's actually incredibly frustrating. It's more like... well, it's exactly what you said, just restless. Edgy. Like I drank three entire pots of terrible, sludgy firehouse coffee and now my skin is vibrating, but there's absolutely no payoff to it. It’s not a good, high mood. If anything, I'm probably way more irritable than usual because I'm so annoyed that I can't just sit in the damn recliner and watch a movie for twenty minutes like a normal person. I just want to relax, and my brain is screaming at me to get up and move. So yeah, no, definitely not euphoric. Just... wired. Constantly, annoyingly wired.",
