    {
      "turn": 5,
      "doctor_question": "Have you ever had a period of at least several days when you felt unusually energetic or high and needed much less sleep than usual?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Several days? Like, a stretch of three or four days feeling energetic on no sleep? No, no way. Like I was saying just a minute ago, it's really the exact opposite. If I go a couple of days without sleep—which, you know, happens in this line of work, like if we get a major incident, a multi-alarm fire or something where everyone gets called in and you're just working on adrenaline and protein bars for 48 hours—I am absolutely wrecked by the end of it. I mean, my body feels like it's been run over by a ladder truck. \n\nThere was this one time last summer, we had this massive brush fire out on the county line, and the wind kept shifting, so we were out there cutting line and hauling hoses for almost three days straight. And yeah, while you're in it, you're moving, you're doing the job, but it's not some... unusually high feeling. It's just pure survival mode. And the second we got back to the bay and peeled our gear off, I was a total zombie. I crashed so hard. \n\nSo, if you mean just sitting around in normal life, off-duty, and suddenly I go on some three-day stretch of feeling fantastic and not needing to sleep? Never. Never happens. If I'm not sleeping, it's because my brain won't shut up and let me rest, like I mentioned, but I feel every single second of that exhaustion. My eyes burn, I get this dull headache right behind my temples, my knees ache... I feel it all. I want the sleep so bad. I'm definitely not walking around feeling energized or high, I'm just dragging myself through the day feeling completely drained but still somehow unable to just sit still. So, no, definitely no periods of feeling like that for days on end. I wish I had that kind of energy, honestly, but no.",
